    "notes": "1. For 'total_accounts_receivable', the primary balance sheet lists 'Trade receivables' and 'Financial services receivables' under current assets. Both are included as they represent amounts due from customers and financing activities. Non-current financial services receivables are not included as they are not expected to be collected within one year.\n2. For 'total_current_liabilities', the sum of 'Financial liabilities (current)', 'Trade payables', and 'Other liabilities (current)' from the primary statement is used. 'Liabilities associated with assets held for sale' (€31 million in 2023) is excluded as it is a separate, non-operational line item.\n3. For 'total_debt_short_term_and_long_term', the sum of 'Financial liabilities' from both the non-current and current sections of the primary balance sheet is used, representing the Group's total borrowings.\n4. 'Short_term_market_securities' is mapped directly to 'Marketable securities and time deposits' from the current assets section.\n5. All values are extracted from the primary consolidated balance sheet on Page 474. The scale is in millions (€ million).",
